# The BINARY store is NOT committed here -- the reviewable text export is (memories.sql,
# written by export.ps1). Three reasons, measured 2026-08-20: ~90% of memory.db is derived
# (FTS5 index + JSON embedding vectors) so 600 KB of binary carried only 52 KB of actual
# knowledge; git cannot merge it, so two branches that both add memories conflict with no
# resolution but discarding one side's memories; and every write rewrites most of the file,
# adding a fresh ~600 KB blob to history per commit. The text export diffs line by line,
# which also means a reviewer can SEE what was added to the assistant's memory.
#
# Consequence to know: memory.db is now local-only. `git clean -xdf` will delete it. It is
# rebuildable from memories.sql (SETUP.md section 9) -- so run export.ps1 before committing,
# or the knowledge exists nowhere shared.
memory.db
memory.db-wal
memory.db-shm

# ...and do NOT ignore the export itself. Listed explicitly so a future broadened *.sql
# rule cannot silently start excluding the only committed copy of the memories.
!memories.sql

# The sqlite-vec index is derived from memory.db's `embeddings` table and is a binary
# that would conflict on merge. Rebuild it with `vec.ps1 index` instead of committing it.
vectors.db
vectors.db-wal
vectors.db-shm

# Local scratch from export/restore or experiments.
*-backup.db
data.sql
memory.sql

# migrate.ps1 takes a timestamped backup before any DDL change. Local safety net,
# not shared state -- delete once the migration is verified.
memory-premigrate-*.db

# Never commit credentials. Embedding providers read keys from the environment or
# from a file outside this repo -- see SETUP.md -> Semantic search.
*.key
.env
secrets.json

# Hook firing log - local evidence only, not shared state.
hook.log

# Provider configuration: names connection files and hosts for THIS machine, so it is
# per-machine state, not shared state. The durable copy lives at ~\.claude\embed.config
# and every project inherits it -- see memconfig.ps1.
embed.config

# Per-session baselines for the Stop-hook memory gate (hook-stop-memory.ps1). Machine- and
# session-local by definition; pruned after 7 days by the SessionStart hook.
.state/
